.policy "ruff-dtz003-call-datetime-utcnow" revision 2
.description "Use datetime.now with a timezone instead of datetime.utcnow; utcnow returns a naive datetime that carries no zone information."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff DTZ003 (flake8-datetimez): `datetime.datetime.utcnow()`, which returns a naive datetime holding UTC, so
// other code reads it as local time. A call followed by `.astimezone()` (through any `.replace(…)`) is not
// reported. Reported at the call. Only in a file that imports datetime.
//   datetime.datetime.utcnow()                   ← DTZ003
//   datetime.datetime.utcnow().astimezone()      not reported
#include "python/datetime.rr"

.violation DTZ003(at: node) code "DTZ003"
    "Replace `utcnow()` with `now(tz=datetime.timezone.utc)` for an aware UTC datetime. Keep `utcnow()` only where the value is mixed with naive datetimes that cannot change too."
    suppress ruff "DTZ003"
DTZ003(c) :- dt_call(c, "datetime.datetime.utcnow"), !then_astimezone(c).
